+/*
+ * 0194: gg_ib_sanitize() clipped every IB to the first 4 KiB GEM page
+ * (room = (GEM_PAGE - offset)/4), so any packet past dword 1024 was never
+ * rewritten. v141 proved it: the 2411-dword UI IB 0x56162000 was sanitized
+ * only up to off=1018, while 0191 pinned the hard stop at off=1359 -- the
+ * 0x8103 GRAS_LRZ_BUFFER_BASE type-4 write. 0192 fired 8 NOPs on OTHER
+ * short IBs and the stop did not move a single dword. Access each dword
+ * through the bounded page cache so the walker can span as many GEM pages
+ * as the IB actually occupies.
+ */
+#define GG_SAN_MAX_DW 8192u
